<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maladhar Basu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1473–1480</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Gunaraj Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maladhar Basu was a Bengali poet from Kulingram in Burdwan who composed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-krishna-vijaya">Sri Krishna Vijaya</a>, a Bengali version of parts of the Bhagavata Purana telling the life of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a>, between 1473 and 1480. He wrote under the patronage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rukunuddin-barbak-shah">Rukunuddin Barbak Shah</a>, who gave him the title Gunaraj Khan, and his work is among the earliest dated texts of Bengali literature.</p></div>
